"""Authored network lessons, based on complete pinned source and named fixtures."""
from lesson_writer import author,CPP
PREFIX='src/org/minima/system/network/'
LIMIT='This lesson explains the inspected source and finite test scope. It does not certify full API parity, live network integration or a working native node. The mapping remains authoritative.'
def lesson(name,purpose,steps,adaptation,driver,evidence,exercise,limits=LIMIT):
 def tests(link):
  if not driver:return evidence
  return link(CPP/'tools'/driver,'Read the differential experiment')+'. '+evidence+' No test was rerun while authoring this lesson; this describes the experiment, not a new passing result.'
 author(PREFIX+name+'.md',purpose,steps,adaptation,tests,exercise,limits)

lesson('p2p/messages/InetSocketAddressIO','Convert peer addresses between Java socket objects and the two JSON forms used by discovery: objects with host/port fields and strings containing host:port.',[
 'Object output visits peers in list order and uses the resolved numeric host address plus the port. An unresolved address can therefore be constructed successfully but fail during output.',
 'String output also uses the resolved numeric address, followed by a colon and the port. Input strings are split on every colon; only the first two pieces become host and port. This is not a general bracketed IPv6 endpoint parser.',
 'Object input casts each item to JSONObject and constructs an address from its host and safeReadInt result. Missing or non-integer port values become zero; a Long outside signed 32-bit range throws.',
 'Each conversion constructs a fresh result list/array. Null containers, null elements, wrong element types, invalid ports and malformed strings fail at the operation that needs them.'
], 'The mapped C++ code reuses InetSocketAddress, ordered JSON and Java integer parsing. It preserves trailing-empty split behavior and checked narrowing instead of treating every JSON number as a port. Shared address/list types model nullable references; generic native exception classes still differ from Java.', 'peer_messages_differential.py','PeerMessagesOracle.java and peer_messages.cpp compare numeric IPv4 forms, IPv6 scopes, unresolved-name equality/hashes, JSON conversion and safeReadInt. Inputs include missing ports, floating values, overflowing integers, extra colons and malformed list elements. Exceptions are collapsed to ERROR; DNS cache and custom JVM networking properties are excluded.','Predict the port for an object containing "port":"9001". Then explain why the string "127.1:9001:ignored" follows a different path.')
lesson('p2p/messages/P2PDoSwap','Carry a swap authorization secret and destination through discovery JSON, while retaining a local client UID that is not transmitted.',[
 'A default instance creates eight random secret bytes and leaves destination and client UID null. The full constructor checks the destination before replacing fields with the supplied references.',
 'toJson creates a do_swap wrapper containing secret, swap_target_host and swap_target_port. It uses getHostString, so a stored hostname can remain a hostname.',
 'readJson updates the secret first if present. It replaces the destination only if both host and port keys exist; absent fields retain their old values.',
 'Reading never updates the local swappingClientUID. If destination construction fails after a valid secret, the changed secret remains: parsing is incremental, not transactional.'
], 'C++ keeps shared MiniData/address objects and an optional UID. It reuses the same JSON and address helpers, and makes the absent destination an explicit checked failure. Random bytes are generated independently in each runtime.', 'peer_messages_differential.py','The swap programs fix the random secret after checking its length, then apply repeated partial JSON reads and setters. Each step captures result, secret, destination, local UID and generated JSON, including state after a failing read. This tests mutation order; it does not compare cryptographic randomness bit for bit.','Start with destination A and secret 0x01. Read a new valid secret plus an out-of-range destination port. Which old fields survive?')
lesson('p2p/messages/P2PWalkLinks','Represent a discovery walk, including its route, direction, joining/client flags, available client slots and authorization secret.',[
 'The default route is a new empty list and the secret has eight random bytes. The target-UID constructor records a local next hop; the path constructor retains the caller’s list and interprets its second Boolean as returning, not joining.',
 'addHopToPath rejects a null new address. Direct mutation through getPathTaken still exposes the underlying list, so that restriction is not enforced on every possible insertion.',
 'getPreviousNode searches for the first address equal to thisAddress and returns the element immediately before it. The first element, a missing address and an empty route return null.',
 'JSON writes a walk_links wrapper with seven protocol fields. The target UID is local and omitted. fromJson applies present fields in order: secret, walk/join/client flags, slots, returning, then path.',
 'A failed later field leaves earlier updates intact. Replacing the path changes which list the walk aliases; existing callers can still hold the former list.'
], 'C++ shared vectors preserve supplied route aliases and address equality uses the Java-compatible adapter. The two Boolean constructor overloads remain distinct by their third argument. Null and bad-type errors are checked but exact Java exception types are not established by the normalized suite.', 'peer_messages_differential.py','Walk experiments exercise all three constructors, aliases through external/returned lists, null paths, duplicate addresses, previous-hop lookup and incremental malformed JSON. Every operation records all flags, route, local target and JSON. The initial secret length is checked before a fixed secret makes comparison deterministic.','For route [A,B,A,C], what does getPreviousNode(A) return? Explain why searching from the end would change the protocol behavior.')
lesson('p2p/messages/P2PSwapLink','Preserve the source inventory entry for an entirely commented-out historical swap-message sketch. This pinned file declares no active Java package, class or method.',[
 'Every line is a comment, including package, imports, class and constructors. Java compilation therefore produces no P2PSwapLink class from this file.',
 'The historical sketch describes secret and destination serialization plus two flags. Because the body is inactive, it is a reading aid rather than executable protocol behavior.',
 'Its commented address stream calls are not the active InetSocketAddressIO JSON API. The working JSON swap message is P2PDoSwap.'
], 'The source map still requires a unique destination for this Java file, and currently records that counterpart as absent. A future inventory-only translation must make the inactive status explicit; reviving the commented design would add behavior rather than preserve the pin.',None,'There is no active class here to instantiate or test. A meaningful future mapping check would verify that its counterpart exists without registering a new protocol type. P2PDoSwap tests cannot establish coverage for this inactive sketch.','Explain the difference between “a Java file exists” and “a Java class is compiled.” Why should a 1:1 file inventory retain this entry?')
lesson('p2p/P2PDB','Store versioned discovery peers in JsonDB using JSON address objects, with detached lists at the public API boundary.',[
 'getPeersList starts with a fresh empty result and defaults a missing peers key to an empty JSONArray. It decodes every stored address before returning.',
 'setPeersList serializes the supplied list immediately and places the completed array in the database. Later changes to the caller’s list do not change stored peers.',
 'Each get constructs new addresses and a new list. Mutating a returned list does not silently save it.',
 'setVersion captures the current P2PParams.VERSION string. getVersion uses the current parameter only when no stored version exists; it does not upgrade older data automatically.'
], 'The translation reuses JsonDB, MiniFile persistence and InetSocketAddressIO. It keeps conversion-before-assignment ordering, so malformed peer output cannot replace the old array with a partially constructed one. This is JSON storage, not a substitute SQL backend.', 'peer_state_differential.py','The db programs change external and extracted lists independently, alter live JSON, round-trip exact wire bytes, truncate reads and change both parameter and stored versions. Each observation freezes the mutable JSON before the next operation. Type failures are normalized; complete filesystem integration is a separate responsibility.','Set peers from list A, append to A, then append to getPeersList(). Which changes require another setPeersList call to persist?')
lesson('p2p/P2PState','Hold discovery’s mutable connection categories, known-peer set, local address and control flags. It is state storage; it does not reconcile the categories automatically.',[
 'Construction creates five separate maps, an empty peer set, wildcard port 9001 address, default MiniData secret and scalar values copied from current P2PParams.',
 'Map setters replace references and getters return those same maps. allLinks is independent of the four category maps; callers must maintain consistency.',
 'getKnownPeers returns the live set, whereas getKnownPeersCopy creates a new list containing the current address references.',
 'The string address setter uses the current GeneralParams.MINIMA_PORT. setLoopDelayToParamValue copies the current global delay; subsequent global changes do not update the state automatically.',
 'toJson removes slash characters from address text, renders four lists in map iteration order, and reports allLinks and known-peer counts separately. Null/replaced maps can make output fail.'
], 'C++ reuses JavaHashMap and SocketAddressSet to preserve address equality and tested iteration/retention behavior. Shared pointers preserve map aliases; separate mutexes protect scalar/reference replacement and peer access. These locks do not prove equivalent whole-program concurrent interleavings.', 'peer_state_differential.py','State programs compare defaults, getters/setters, aliases, null replacements, map insertion/removal order, set equality/resizing, copied lists and JSON after every operation. Special non-comparable hash collision cases compare membership only. Greeting shuffle order is normalized as a permutation, and concurrent mutation is excluded.','Put a peer in inLinks only. What should numAllLinks report? Identify which component must later reconcile the two maps.')
lesson('p2p/messages/P2PGreeting','Advertise a node’s discovery capabilities and peers. Its equals method is deliberately much weaker than full message equality.',[
 'The state constructor copies in/out map values and known peers, captures current port and connection limits, optionally appends the local address when accepting inbound links, then shuffles known peers.',
 'The short and full explicit constructors retain supplied lists. The short constructor marks the node as not accepting inbound links.',
 'fromJSON reads the inner greeting object, not its outer wrapper. It always reads port, acceptance and known peers, and only reads in/out links and client counts when accepting.',
 'toJson always emits port, acceptance and known peers; it emits the extra link/count fields only for an accepting node, then wraps everything under greeting.',
 'equals returns true for self before touching fields, false for other types/null, then compares only port, acceptance and known-peer count. Different peer contents can compare equal.'
], 'C++ retains shared explicit-constructor lists and creates new state-constructor lists. Native shuffle uses independent entropy, so a seeded Java shuffle sequence is not claimed. The typed equals pointer API preserves self/null short circuits and the narrow three-field comparison.', 'peer_state_differential.py','The fixture exercises constructors, list aliases, JSON defaults and wrong types, serialization and equality. An explicit case uses different peer contents with equal sizes, and another sets knownPeers null before self-comparison. State-constructor known peers are sorted for comparison; equality alone is never treated as proof that serialized messages match.','Construct two greetings with the same port and one different known peer each. Can equals return true while their JSON differs? Show why.')
lesson('p2p/params/P2PParams','Define mutable process-wide discovery defaults: capacity targets, delays, version, logging and the initially empty default-node list.',[
 'The pinned version is 1.1. Defaults include 50 stored peers, five target links, 100 non-P2P links and two minimum client connections.',
 'Delays are integer milliseconds: main loop/save/metrics 600000, loop variability 30000, inbound check 3600000, walk expiry 10000 and authorization expiry 300000. Hash-rate refresh is 43200000.',
 'DEFAULT_NODE_LIST is an empty Arrays.asList list. Its reference is replaceable, but the initial list has fixed size; an append fails rather than supplying a seed peer.',
 'Consumers may copy scalars at construction or consult them later. Changing these fields is not a broadcast update to every existing P2PState.'
], 'C++ uses static signed integers and a nullable log-level value. JavaList models fixed-size structural restrictions, while shared ownership allows replacement and aliasing. No fallback discovery node has been invented.', 'peer_state_differential.py','The params branch snapshots each field and tries append, clear and element replacement on the original empty list. Other branches change LOOP_DELAY and inspect existing versus reset state. Test-mode application has additional explicit scalar-copy and list-alias assertions.','Why does replacing DEFAULT_NODE_LIST with a growable list differ from appending to its initial value?')
lesson('p2p/params/P2PTestParams','Provide a mutable test configuration and explicitly copy selected values into P2PParams when setTestParams is called.',[
 'Test defaults use DEBUG, two non-P2P links, a five-second loop, three-second variability, one-minute save/inbound/hash refresh, five-second walk expiry and thirty-second metrics.',
 'The test default-node list contains minima_one:9001 and has fixed size. The metrics URL is a test field but is not copied into P2PParams.',
 'setTestParams assigns the node-list reference first and then copies the listed scalar fields in source order. VERSION and PEERS_LIST_SIZE are not assigned.',
 'Later edits to a copied scalar require another application. Element changes through the shared list are visible through both configurations, while replacing the test list does not change the active reference until application.'
], 'A lazily initialized singleton settings object models Java static fields and defers host resolution until test configuration is accessed. The active list shares JavaList ownership, preserving fixed-size behavior and subsequent reference replacement.', 'peer_state_differential.py','The testParams programs inspect defaults before application, modify each integer at signed boundaries, apply repeatedly and compare aliases. Explicit assertions require DEBUG/5000 defaults, the minima_one entry, errors on structural edits and visible element replacement through the active alias. Null list replacement and log-level changes are also exercised.','Apply test settings, replace the test list, then append through the old active list. Which list will the next application install?')
lesson('p2p2/P2P2DB','Maintain the second discovery system’s live peer-string list alongside JsonDB persistence and a first-startup flag.',[
 'getAllKnownPeers returns the same mutable ArrayList. addPeerToAllKnown checks list membership, appends only a new value, logs either outcome and returns whether it added.',
 'saveDB first converts the live list to all_known_peers in JSON, then calls saveObjectDirect. A failed disk write can therefore leave changed in-memory JSON.',
 'loadDB first invokes loadObjectSlow on this object, clears the existing live list, then casts and appends JSON entries one at a time. A late non-string leaves earlier entries already appended.',
 'The list object survives loading, so old callers observe its cleared/repopulated contents. Direct readDataStream affects JsonDB data without automatically rebuilding this separate list.',
 'first_startup defaults to true and is changed only by its setter; adding a peer does not implicitly clear it.'
], 'C++ reuses JsonDB virtual load/save dispatch, MiniFile and MiniUtil string-list conversion. A shared vector of optional strings preserves list identity and null values. UTF-16-compatible string comparison supports duplicate detection; native log text lacks Java logger prefixes.', 'p2p2_db_differential.py','P2P2DBOracle and p2p2_db call load/save through a JsonDB reference, retain an alias, compare wire and file bytes, and inject absent/truncated/malformed files and a blocked output path. A JSON list with valid strings, null and a later integer tests partial append before failure. Errors and log prefixes are normalized.','After loading ["first",null,7,"last"], what should the retained list alias show when the integer cast fails?')
lesson('rpc/Authorizer','Parse the pinned Basic authorization format and return a JSON decision using the main password and configured RPC users.',[
 'Retrieve UserDB and count RPC users before entering the parsing try/catch. Missing database state can therefore escape instead of becoming a normal invalid-credentials reply.',
 'Only auth style basic is supported. Search for the case-sensitive substring Basic anywhere in the header, decode everything after it with the Basic Base64 decoder, decode UTF-8 and trim Java control/space characters.',
 'Split decoded text at its first colon. The remaining password may itself contain colons. Record username before checking credentials.',
 'For username minima, authentication disabled or an equal configured password yields valid=true and mode=write. Failed main-user credentials return the minimal valid=false object.',
 'Additional users are checked only when main authentication is enabled. Iterate all matching records without breaking, so a later duplicate can replace mode. An unmatched extra user retains username with valid=false; a caught malformed record discards that partial reply.',
 'Parsing exceptions are logged and return the minimal rejection. Mode selection here does not prove that CMDHandler enforces read-only command execution.'
], 'C++ reuses actual UserDB, MiniString and the checked Base64 adapter. The one-argument method needs a MinimaDB binding; the direct overload accepts the database explicitly for fixtures. Logging currently uses native diagnostic output and full exception/log parity remains open.', 'network_utilities_differential.py','NetworkUtilityOracle and network_utilities compare exact decision JSON for prefixed/case-varied headers, padding errors, missing colons, Unicode credentials, duplicate users, null/wrong-type records and auth disabled. The driver also exhaustively varies short Base64 strings. It does not execute an RPC server or wallet command.','Why can a later malformed user record turn an earlier successful match into the minimal rejection object?')
lesson('minima/NIOTraffic','Keep synchronized byte totals and independently accumulated per-category traffic statistics.',[
 'reset captures the current time, clears both totals and replaces both breakdown tables. It does not preserve old table entries.',
 'addToTotalRead and addToTotalWrite change only overall counters. addReadBytes and addWriteBytes change only a named breakdown entry: the apparent total updates in those methods are commented out.',
 'A category starts at zero, then adds the signed amount. Java long arithmetic wraps on overflow and accepts negative increments.',
 'getBreakdown enumerates each Hashtable and formats values with MiniFormat.formatSize into reads/writes JSON. Null category keys fail through Hashtable rules.'
], 'C++ holds a mutex around each operation, uses JavaHashtable for tested UTF-16 key enumeration and performs addition through unsigned arithmetic plus bit reinterpretation to obtain Java wraparound without C++ signed-overflow undefined behavior. resetAt is a native fixture aid for deterministic timestamps.', 'network_utilities_differential.py','Traffic programs interleave resets, total and category additions with zero/negative/extreme signed values, collision-heavy keys and Unicode. After each step the fixture compares result, totals and formatted ordered JSON, and finally the chosen start time. This sequential experiment does not establish concurrent interleaving equivalence.','After addReadBytes("greeting",100), what is totalRead? Explain why automatically adding to the total here would double-count some callers.')
lesson('rpc/Server','Define the minimal base contract for port-bearing servers: retain the configured integer and require a shutdown implementation.',[
 'Construction assigns the supplied port directly. No range validation or socket binding occurs in this class.',
 'getPort returns the configured value, including zero when the caller requests an ephemeral operating-system port.',
 'shutdown is abstract. Listener creation, actual bound-port discovery, handler lifecycle and cleanup belong to concrete subclasses.'
], 'The C++ base retains a signed 32-bit port, a pure virtual shutdown and a virtual destructor for deletion through a base pointer. The native HTTPServer separately exposes the actual bound port; getPort continues to mean the configured port.', 'http_server_differential.py','The listener fixture checks getPort for automatic and manual startup at port zero and for a bind collision. It separately observes the ephemeral bound port and normalizes that OS-chosen number. Thus a working bind does not change the base object’s configured port.','Why should getPort return zero after a successful ephemeral bind? Which observation would a test need to connect to that listener?')
lesson('rpc/HTTPServer','Accept TCP connections and delegate each accepted socket to an independently running request handler.',[
 'Java construction optionally starts a listener thread. run binds a ServerSocket at the configured port and logs startup before entering the running loop.',
 'Each loop accepts one socket, calls getSocketHandler on the listener thread, then starts its returned Runnable in a daemon thread named Socket Handler @ followed by the configured port.',
 'The handler is independent of the next accept operation. A slow request should not prevent another connection’s handler from running.',
 'shutdown sets running false before closing the server socket. The resulting socket failure is logged only if the server still considers itself running.',
 'BindException, SocketException and IOException have separate catch behavior. Other runtime failures and Java Errors are not caught by this source body; handler failures occur on the handler thread.'
], 'C++ starts only after derived shared ownership exists, avoiding a worker using a half-owned object. It reuses POSIX sockets with default dual-stack binding and a wakeup pipe/poll loop so shutdown interrupts waiting reliably. Handler closures retain accepted sockets; detached threads model Java daemon handlers. A separate bound-port field supports ephemeral-port tests.', 'http_server_differential.py','HTTPServerOracle and http_server use actual listener sockets and a binary reversing handler. One connection is held open while four others complete, then the held request completes; factory/completion counts and concurrent activity are observed. Automatic/manual startup, port collision logs and shutdown completion are compared. The configured port remains distinct from the normalized ephemeral port.','Identify whether an exception from getSocketHandler occurs in the listener thread or the request thread. Why does that distinction affect which loop survives?')
lesson('rpc/CMDHandler','Handle exactly one socket request, turn its path or POST body into a command string, and write the pinned HTTP-style response.',[
 'Read the first line as text, tokenize method/path, uppercase the method, remove at most one leading and trailing slash, URL-decode the path, then trim it. Even methods other than GET/POST proceed through this parser.',
 'Default authorization is write access, but authentication enabled or a nonempty RPC user list makes it invalid until an Authorization header succeeds. Header matching uses case-sensitive substring searches, and later matching headers replace earlier values.',
 'On rejection write the 401 body then throw into the outer request logger. Otherwise POST allocates contentlength characters and reads UTF-16 character units, not raw byte counts. A short body retains zero-filled unused characters.',
 'Run CommandRunner on the selected string. One result is unwrapped; zero or multiple results remain an array. A caught command exception leaves the default status=false JSON. The read/write mode enforcement block is commented out in the pin.',
 'Write 200 headers with optional CRLF, UTF-8 content byte length and a final body newline that is not included in that length. Close the request resources afterward.',
 'An exact quit command sets a flag before execution and calls process halt after cleanup. The ordinary response suite deliberately does not establish this process-lifecycle path.'
], 'C++ reuses SocketCharacterReader for incremental UTF-8/UTF-16 behavior, JavaURLDecoder, integer parsing and CommandRunner. Socket shared ownership replaces separate Java stream/socket objects. PrintWriter-style output IO failures are swallowed. Full cleanup failure order, logger text and Main quit integration remain review boundaries.', 'cmd_handler_differential.py','The experiment uses actual Java/native HTTPServer and CMDHandler over TCP and actual mapped commands. It varies LF/CR/CRLF, malformed URL/UTF-8, duplicate/case-varied headers, authentication configurations, short/long UTF-16 body counts and multibyte fragments around the reader boundary. Response bytes and lengths are compared after validating and normalizing only the wall-clock Date. Some diagnostic details are compared by failure site rather than exact text.','For POST body π😄, compare UTF-8 bytes with UTF-16 units. Why would reading Content-Length as bytes silently change this pinned behavior?')
lesson('webhooks/NotifyManager','Queue notifications, call an in-process listener and deliver filtered copies to configured webhook URLs.',[
 'Construction loads a hook list from UserDB. PostEvent queues the supplied JSON object by reference, so changes before processing are visible.',
 'addHook excludes a new empty string and duplicates, then saves the list even when nothing was added. removeHook and clearHooks also save after mutation. getAllWebHooks creates a detached string list and fails on null elements.',
 'For NOTIFY_POST, retrieve the notification and capture its event string before invoking the optional listener. The listener receives the original Message and can mutate the JSON or replace the message’s notify field.',
 'After the listener, serialize the originally captured notification object and take a hook snapshot. Listener edits to that object affect the body; the previously captured event still controls filtering.',
 'Split each hook at its first #. A hook without # returns from the entire delivery operation, preventing later hooks from running. Check running before each send; an empty filter matches every event, otherwise use case-sensitive substring matching.',
 'A listener Exception is logged and delivery normally continues; an error while logging can itself interrupt it. A POST Exception is optionally logged with notifications disabled to avoid recursive notification logging. Snapshot hooks isolate later hook-list changes during delivery.'
], 'C++ reuses MessageProcessor, shared Message/JSONObject values, UserDB UTF-16 hook conversion and RPCClient. Required listener and service receivers make the still-unfinished Main integration explicit. A recursive hook lock permits inspected callback reentry; atomic stop/log flags prevent data races without claiming every Java interleaving.', 'notify_manager_differential.py','NotifyManagerOracle and notify_manager compare FIFO retained message identity, mutations before processing, listener edits/replacement/errors, hook snapshots, malformed-hook early return, stop, database rebinding/failure and UTF-16 filters including surrogate halves. Java’s actual RPCClient meets a controlled HttpURLConnection; native delivery uses a controlled receiver. This is delivery logic evidence, not a claim that real external webhook requests were sent.','A listener changes event from MINING to SECOND. Which value chooses filters, and which value appears in the posted JSON? Trace the two capture points.')
lesson('p2p/UtilFuncs','Look up discovery links by address and select a random address without changing the input list.',[
 'searchLinksMapForAddress iterates map keys in their collection order. On the first equal address it immediately returns P2PFunctions.getNIOCLientInfo for that UID, even if the client lookup returns null.',
 'getClientFromInetAddress searches inLinks, outLinks, not-accepting P2P links, then non-P2P links, proceeding to the next category when the preceding result is null.',
 'selectRandomAddress returns null for an empty list. A one-element list uses index zero without consuming a random number; larger lists use nextInt(size).',
 'A null map value fails when equality is invoked. A null selected list element can be returned normally; no address validation is added here.'
], 'C++ reuses peer map/address equality and the existing JavaRandom48 generator. Shared state and client-info objects preserve lifetimes; seeded fixtures can compare both selections and subsequent random draws, exposing accidental extra consumption.', 'p2p_functions_differential.py','The map-precedence/search groups include missing client UIDs, null keys/values and multiple categories. Random-selection programs use six seeds, empty/single/multiple lists and explicit bounded draws afterward. Invalid bounds and null lists produce normalized ERROR. This observes generator consumption, not just whether a result belongs to the list.','If the first matching UID has no active client but a second matching UID does, does searchLinksMapForAddress inspect the second?')
lesson('p2p/P2PFunctions','Bridge discovery policy to NIO connection messages, cached interface names, peer exclusions, logging and availability checks.',[
 'Cache and return the live local-hostname set. Only interface SocketException triggers the fallback names localhost, 127.0.0.1 and 127.0.1.1. The invalid-peer set is separate and mutable; adding an existing entry avoids another log.',
 'checkConnect rejects an explicitly invalid host:port first, then strings with more than one colon. Its local-address rule is a literal prefix list, including broad prefixes such as 172. and 198.; it is not a CIDR parser.',
 'Unless ALLOW_ALL_IP is enabled, a local prefix rejects connection. A caught error during this local check is logged and processing continues.',
 'Reject a matching host/port only when its client is still connecting. Already connected entries do not trigger that particular guard. A permitted request posts NIO_CONNECT and returns true; direct connect bypasses these policy checks.',
 'Connection queries build NIOClientInfo lists; sends serialize JSON as MiniString in MSG_P2P and an empty UID broadcasts. Logging levels have explicit equality rules, not a simple numeric threshold.',
 'isNetAvailable opens the configured source URL, connects, opens input and closes it. Ordinary exceptions yield false; this probes that operation, not every peer route.'
], 'The translation reuses NIOManager, message framing, JavaStringSet and native interface/HTTP adapters. Required runtime lookup and optional platform/log receivers keep source policy separate from external effects. The sibling blocking network design was not substituted.', 'p2p_functions_differential.py','The actual helper methods run on controlled managers with real native maps/queues and codecs. Programs compare invalid/local/IPv6 ordering, pending versus connected clients, send packets, log bodies and live cache aliases. A separate loopback HTTP experiment checks response/redirect paths; the default public HTTPS provider and full Main bindings remain outside that evidence.','Why can a hostname beginning localhost.evil be rejected by this exact source? Explain why replacing the rule with a standards-based IP parser would change a 1:1 port.')
lesson('p2p/WalkLinksFuncs','Route discovery walks, turn completed walks into connection attempts and generate swap requests when link capacity is exceeded.',[
 'Filter a chosen link map against every address already in the route. Incoming/outgoing walk handling first appends the sender address, then selects a remaining neighbor. Continue only while route length is below nine and a next hop exists.',
 'An exhausted incoming-link walk appends this node, marks returning and, for a client walk, records max non-P2P capacity minus current not-accepting peers. Response routing uses the previous occurrence in the recorded route.',
 'An exhausted outgoing-link walk can request an inbound swap only when inLinks exceeds the target. The source chooses nextInt(numberOfKeys-1), excluding the final key and failing when that bound is zero. The original secret and first route address are reused.',
 'A returned scale-out walk attempts the last route address while below target, stops after a permitted connection, and removes the attempted address by value. With duplicates, remove deletes its first equal occurrence rather than necessarily the final element.',
 'A returned load-balance walk uses its last address unless it is this node. When overloaded, generate at most min(available remote slots, local maximum/2) messages for the first selected map keys, with new eight-byte secrets.',
 'Helpers may return null, an empty list, or messages. Connection requests are also posted as side effects; an empty returned list does not mean no work occurred.'
], 'C++ reuses shared route lists, peer map enumeration, JavaRandom48 and DoSwap/WalkLinks codecs. Separate seeded random streams preserve selection order; signed slot subtraction is explicit wraparound. Actual NIO connection posting remains visible through the existing manager.', 'walk_links_differential.py','P2PFunctionsOracle and p2p_functions execute every walk helper and snapshot route mutations, return flags, slots, logs and posted connections. Cases vary lengths around nine, zero/one/many keys, duplicate paths, null receivers and signed capacities. Explicit assertions require one-key swap selection to fail and successful choices to exclude the final key. Only newly random secret bytes are canonicalized while lengths/reuse are retained.','For [A,B,A], trace the first failed attempt at A and the list after remove(A). Why is pop_back an incorrect translation?')
lesson('p2p/SwapLinksFunctions','Turn connection and greeting events into discovery state transitions, authenticated IP discovery and capacity-balancing walks.',[
 'onConnected inserts the peer into non-P2P links first. Incoming connections use host with port zero for duplicate detection; duplicates produce a disconnect message but are still inserted. Other connections produce a greeting and, if the host is unknown, a new twelve-byte IP-request secret.',
 'processGreeting removes the provisional entry, marks the actual NIO client’s greeting flag when Main exists, then categorizes an accepting peer into in/out links or a non-accepting peer into the not-accepting map. Excess outgoing capacity posts disconnect after insertion.',
 'An accepting greeting clears the returned noconnect flag. A discovery connection clears its state flag and disconnects after classification. The computed addtoknown Boolean is unused; this method does not add that address to known peers.',
 'Disconnect removes the UID from four maps in source order. Failure in a later map does not undo earlier removals; allLinks is not touched here.',
 'IP requests echo the secret and sender host. Responses change the local address, mark host set and remove self from known peers only when the secret matches.',
 'Scale-out and scale-in requests select a current outgoing neighbor and create walks with different direction/join flags. Load balancing requires excess non-accepting peers plus inbound links; its number of identical walk messages uses integer division by max P2P capacity.'
], 'Shared state, existing message codecs and actual NIO client flags are reused. A required Main-presence receiver distinguishes absent Main from a missing manager. Native wrapP2PMsg retains its input JSON alias; OS-generated secrets and shuffle order are not forced to match Java randomness.', 'swap_links_differential.py','The shared fixture captures complete peer maps, NIO greeting flags, disconnect queues and returned message JSON after each call. It tests duplicate incoming peers, greeting capacity boundaries, partial map failures, IP-secret mismatch, invalid ports, zero divisors and wrapper aliasing. Random secret lengths/equality relationships and known-peer permutation are retained while bytes/order are canonicalized.','Why must a duplicate incoming connection still appear in noneP2PLinks even though its returned action requests disconnection?')
lesson('p2p2/P2P2Functions','Provide the second discovery subsystem’s connection helpers with its own invalid-peer set and local-address cache.',[
 'The hostname cache and invalid-peer set belong to P2P2 independently of the original P2P class. Fallback interface names and address-prefix/colon checks follow the same source rules.',
 'checkConnect rejects its own invalid entries, multiple-colon endpoints and disallowed local prefixes before checking pending connections. Matching already connected clients are not rejected by the pending guard.',
 'Permitted checks post NIO_CONNECT; direct connect and disconnect go straight to NIOManager. Queries return all or only connected client-info records.',
 'P2P2 logs its local-rejection and successful-request messages without the original P2P debug-level gate. The availability probe still opens and closes the source HTTPS URL.'
], 'C++ reuses identical P2PFunctions transport/query/parser implementations while retaining separate P2P2 sets and cache plus distinct policy log text. This is selective reuse of compatible behavior, not aliasing the two subsystems’ mutable state.', 'p2p2_runtime_differential.py','The helper groups reuse the original connection-policy corpus but invoke actual P2P2 methods. An explicit independence operation mutates the old subsystem and verifies the new cache/set remain separate. Pending/connected queries, availability and queue/log effects are observed with controlled external receivers.','If old P2P marks an endpoint invalid, is it automatically invalid for P2P2? Identify the fields that make the answer precise.')
lesson('p2p2/P2P2Manager','Translate the active behavior of an unfinished upstream discovery manager without inventing the algorithms its comments propose.',[
 'Construction queues INIT and schedules a five-minute fast loop and six-hour slow loop. shutdown stops the processor and logs; the declared SHUTDOWN message has no matching active branch.',
 'INIT logs and adds the literal source strings 324.45.45.45:9901 twice and 324.45.45.45:9902 once through P2P2DB. These are stored peer strings, not successful network connections. It then reads first-startup even though that conditional body is inactive.',
 'FAST_LOOP schedules its next timer before checking network availability. Offline returns immediately. When below the desired connection count, it selects a peer but never connects: the connection statement is commented out.',
 'Random selection returns an empty string for no peers and otherwise uses a fresh Random for an index. Null entries may be selected.',
 'SLOW_LOOP and checkWhichConnect contain no active work. convertOldP2P reads each old address’s host/port but neither fills nor saves a new list.'
], 'C++ uses existing MessageProcessor, P2P2DB and JavaRandom48 with explicit database receivers. It preserves source no-ops and lookup order, including effects before later failures. Completing the intended new discovery design would be a separate behavior change, not a faithful translation.', 'p2p2_runtime_differential.py','P2P2RuntimeOracle and p2p2_runtime record database access order, inserted peers, queued/timer messages, shutdown state and old database contents. They inject lookup failures and malformed first-startup data, vary online/connectivity counts and exercise inactive branches. Fresh multi-peer choices are compared by membership and distribution bounds, not identical random sequences.','Why should a FAST_LOOP test expect another timer but no NIO_CONNECT message even when the node has zero connections?')
lesson('NetworkManager','Own discovery, NIO transport and optional RPC services, select the host address and summarize their status.',[
 'Construction calculates the host, starts P2P or a dummy processor, creates NIO, then starts P2P2 or its dummy, and finally optional RPC. This source order matters when startup fails after earlier workers have begun.',
 'Host selection returns immediately for an explicitly configured host. Otherwise start at 127.0.0.1, skip down/loopback interfaces, accept IPv4-looking addresses and prefer the first one on an interface whose display name starts wl. Without that preferred interface, later suitable addresses replace earlier choices.',
 'Status retrieves UserDB even though the returned object is unused, then reports host/ports and pending/connected counts. Full status adds discovery configuration and formatted traffic.',
 'Traffic rates divide signed byte totals by elapsed whole minutes, forcing a zero divisor to one. Negative durations retain Java Duration and integer-division semantics; the clock is not clamped to startup time.',
 'startRPC creates only when absent; stopRPC shuts down before clearing its reference. shutdownNetwork sets the flag, stops RPC, posts NIO shutdown, then stops both discovery processors.',
 'Completion uses ordered short-circuit checks on all three processors. hardShutDown catches the NIO operation’s Exception and then stops discovery; it is a different sequence from normal shutdown.'
], 'C++ reuses the actual mapped managers and HTTPServer/CMDHandler. Factories establish shared ownership before workers start; weak owner callbacks avoid permanent cycles. Native destructor/join cleanup also covers partial construction. Required database/Main services remain explicit, and the owner shutdown flag is kept separate from NIO’s Main shutdown receiver.', 'network_manager_differential.py','NetworkManagerOracle and network_manager compare real host-interface selection and status with actual NIO maps/traffic, signed rate extremes, configured-host bypass and unused database lookup failure order. Start-date text is normalized and elapsed values avoid live minute boundaries. This driver does not prove constructor/soft-hard lifecycle parity; native integration checks are a separate category.','Why must getStatus still call getUserDB even though it never reads the returned UserDB? Consider a receiver that throws.')
lesson('minima/NIOClient','Maintain one connection’s metadata and incremental length-prefixed byte transport across nonblocking reads and writes.',[
 'The connecting constructor creates identity/host metadata and captures the manager but leaves buffers and queues uninitialized. The connected constructor also allocates two 8192-byte buffers, the temporary read array, outgoing queue and connection timestamps.',
 'sendData holds the queue lock, checks key validity, appends the supplied data, enables read/write interest and wakes the selector. Failure after append leaves the queued item present.',
 'handleRead first performs one channel read, rejects EOF, accounts the byte count and returns on zero. After flipping the buffer it reads a signed big-endian four-byte length only when all four bytes are available.',
 'Reject lengths above 256 MiB; other invalid lengths fail later through allocation/copy rules. Accumulate payload across reads. At exact completion post NIO_NEWMSG with UID, current full address and payload, then clear the accumulation and update last-read time. A posting failure occurs before that cleanup.',
 'handleWrite fills available space with queued frames, writing each four-byte length before its payload. Oversized queued data is removed and logged, then the fill loop stops. It writes the prepared buffer once, accounts bytes, removes write interest only when all buffered/current/queued data is gone, and compacts remaining bytes.',
 'Metadata includes separate socket port and advertised Minima port; full address prefers the latter unless it is -1. disconnect cancels the key before closing the socket within one Exception catch, so cancel failure can skip close.'
], 'The translation reuses FastByteArrayStream, NIOTraffic, Message and socket/key interfaces with explicit buffer position/limit state. Shared queued data and runtime receivers retain lifetimes; metadata and queue locks plus atomic tracing avoid native data races. POSIX transport and selector integration are separate layers; generic diagnostic text remains incomplete.', 'nio_client_differential.py','NIOClientOracle bypasses Main startup but executes the original client constructors/methods on controlled Channel/Key objects. Both harnesses compare full buffer hashes/positions, accumulated/current data, queue snapshots, traffic, posted messages, wake/interest/cancel effects and metadata after each operation. Cases split headers and payloads around 8192, throttle writes to zero/one byte, inject failures and test invalid/empty frames. Random UID format and clock effects are checked without equal entropy; errors are normalized.','If posting a completed frame throws, which fields still describe the completed payload? Explain why resetting them in a finally block would change the next read.')
lesson('minima/NIOClientInfo','Expose a mostly copied connection summary while retaining selected live access to the underlying NIOClient.',[
 'The explicit UID/host/port constructor marks connected true but stores no underlying client. Welcome, advertised port and validity keep their defaults.',
 'The client-based constructor retains the client reference and copies welcome, greeting validity, host, ports, UID, incoming flag and the supplied connected flag.',
 'Ordinary metadata getters use copied fields. getTimeConnected and getExtraData delegate to the live client, and setExtrasData modifies that same client.',
 'toJSON writes copied metadata and includes a formatted connected timestamp only when a client exists. Thus a later host change can be invisible while a later connection-time change is visible.',
 'An explicit summary can serialize normally but its live-delegating getters fail because no client was supplied.'
], 'C++ uses shared ownership for the retained client and optional strings for nullable copied fields. This is intentionally neither a wholly frozen snapshot nor a wholly live view. Returning value copies of NIOClientInfo does not sever the underlying shared client.', 'nio_client_differential.py','The client experiment repeatedly creates summaries, mutates original client metadata and timestamps, and writes extras through the summary. It captures summary JSON, live time/extras and copied validity separately. Explicit and null-client construction cases identify operations that do or do not require the underlying client.','After creating an info object, change client host, validity and extra data. Which info observations change without constructing another info object?')
lesson('minima/RelayPolicy','Apply local forwarding limits to output counts and the amount of state retained by output coins.',[
 'Check the main transaction’s number of outputs against MAX_RELAY_OUTPUTCOINS, then the burn transaction’s count. Equality with the limit is allowed; a failure logs which transaction exceeded it.',
 'For each transaction, count only outputs whose storeState flag is true. Multiply that count by calculateStateSize; coins not retaining state contribute zero to this policy estimate.',
 'Add main and burn costs using signed long behavior. Reject only when total exceeds the supplied maximum and log the detailed counts/sizes.',
 'checkAllPolicies short-circuits output-count failure. A failed state-size check logs an additional forwarding-failure message. Passing these local relay policies is not complete consensus validation.'
], 'C++ reuses Transaction state-size calculations and preserves tested signed multiplication/addition with explicit unsigned arithmetic. The current counterpart returns the Boolean policy results but omits the Java log calls. This is a concrete remaining behavioral gap, especially if logging itself fails.', 'consensus_differential.py','The check fixture deserializes the same Java-created TxPoW/MMR bytes in both runtimes and calls checkAllPolicies with (output limit,state limit) pairs (64,65536), (2,128) and (-1,-1), alongside other checker calls. It compares returned outcomes; the driver strips Java logger lines. Consequently those comparisons cannot validate the missing native relay logs or their exception effects.','If two outputs store state and a third does not, why is the state charge twice the transaction’s state size rather than three times?')
lesson('p2p/P2PPeersChecker','Maintain candidate and verified peers by checking their greetings against network mode and available local chain history.',[
 'The two getters expose live sets. Admission ignores known candidates, caps the unverified set, and when verified capacity is full admits a new candidate only on the source’s roughly ten-percent random branch. Admitting queues a check.',
 'ADDPEERS retrieves the local-address cache even though its returned set is unused, applies prefix/IPv6 checks, and permits a bypass with ALLOW_ALL_IP.',
 'CHECKPEERS reads optional force and forcelog separately. Force permits a ping without any connected clients; otherwise a disconnected node schedules a one-minute retry without pinging.',
 'A greeting must match TEST versus non-TEST mode and contain nonempty 50block/50hash fields. With enough local history, the referenced node must exist and have the same hash. No local tip or a tip below that height logs inability to check but does not itself invalidate the greeting.',
 'Success removes the unverified entry, may randomly evict a verified peer and notify its removal, then removes/readds this address and posts P2P_ADD_PEER. Failure of a previously verified peer moves it to unverified and schedules a thirty-minute retry; failure of an unverified peer removes it outright. Both failure paths notify the parent.',
 'LOOP queues checks when online and always reschedules six hours later. FORCEFULLCHECK enables forcelog on queued checks, not force: it does not bypass the connected-client prerequisite. INIT has no active work.'
], 'C++ reuses SocketAddressSet, actual NIO ping and TxPoWTreeNode lookups. A weak parent receiver prevents the parent/checker ownership cycle; database tip access is explicit. Random admission/eviction remains independent across runtimes, and missing receivers may fail after earlier set mutations.', 'peers_checker_differential.py','PeersCheckerOracle and peers_checker use Java-created chain identities and a real loopback responder carrying actual serialized Greetings. They compare exact request bytes, traffic, sets, parent messages, timer delays and log bodies for good/wrong/future/missing chain data, test-mode mismatch and receiver failures. Random admissions are checked statistically and by state invariants; arbitrary multi-peer random eviction order is not claimed.','Why does FORCEFULLCHECK still schedule a one-minute retry when no peers are connected? Distinguish force from forcelog.')
lesson('p2p/P2PManager','Coordinate the original discovery subsystem: initialization, connection categories, JSON message routing, periodic balancing and peer persistence.',[
 'Construction creates state, optionally applies test parameters, creates the checker and schedules loop/connectivity/save timers. INIT later loads saved peers, records their initial count, optionally parses configured addnodes only when empty, and queues forced checker requests before selecting a connection.',
 'Initialization copies host/no-connect/capacity settings into state. Connection preference is the source firstgo branch, configured root, random saved peer, then discovery. Discovery requires its state flag and a running processor; it tries at most three pings, waits five seconds after null replies, decodes peers-list, and populates known plus verified sets on success. With no defaults it rate-limits the explanatory log.',
 'CONNECTED inserts allLinks before invoking swap helpers; DISCONNECTED removes allLinks then categories. NOCONNECT removes the failed address and moves matching inbound entries to not-accepting using allLinks values.',
 'JSON routing first resolves the client. Missing clients request disconnect. The swap_links_p2p object uses independent ordered if blocks for greeting, IP request/response, not-accepting, walk and swap, so one object can trigger several actions. DoSwap schedules connect then disconnect; no extra secret-verification gate exists in this branch.',
 'The periodic loop chooses a delay based on outgoing capacity, removes self from known peers, and connects directly, grows outgoing links, requests inbound links or balances clients as appropriate. Empty known peers trigger saved-peer checks and discovery. Connectivity assessment marks a node non-accepting only for the source’s particular empty/nonempty category combination.',
 'Returned walks are routed toward their start or consumed there; outgoing walks dispatch by direction. sendMessages executes returned actions in list order, wrapping JSON under swap_links_p2p and ignoring null messages. Earlier effects remain if a later send fails.',
 'Health checks clear nonessential queued messages only above fifty, preserving the three named timer types. Persistence replaces stored peers only when nonempty and at least half the initial count. Shutdown stores version, updates peers, stops checker, logs, then stops itself. Status and haveAnyPeers use their explicit query/short-circuit order.'
], 'The translation reuses P2PState, checker, walk/swap helpers, P2PDB, NIOManager and JavaRandom48. Factories create shared ownership before workers start and the checker holds a weak parent. Database save/tip/time callbacks are explicit runtime boundaries. State constructed before test-parameter application keeps that source ordering; independent entropy and shuffled peer lists are compared only within stated scope.', 'p2p_manager_differential.py','P2PManagerOracle and p2p_manager manually execute actual manager methods on unstarted fixtures, capturing state, checker queues, NIO packets, timers, logs and DB changes after each operation. Cases cover parsing, capacity/persistence thresholds, overload at fifty, malformed multi-field JSON, signed delays, null maps and partial failures. Packet lengths remain checked while random secrets and shuffled known peers are canonicalized. The separate p2p_discovery_differential.py uses actual loopback ping bytes and real retry pauses, including dropped replies and the three-attempt cap. Neither fixture alone proves complete Main lifecycle integration.','A greeting and notAcceptingMsg arrive in the same wrapper. Trace both blocks and explain why replacing the independent if statements with else-if changes final state.')

lesson('minima/NIOServer','Own the nonblocking listener and connected-client registry, using selector events to move framed bytes and report connection lifecycle events.',[
 'Construction only stores configuration and creates queues. run marks itself running, opens/binds the listener and selector, then posts SERVERSTARTED. A bind IOException logs and halts the process with exit code zero; other outer exceptions finish the run method.',
 'register and disconnect append under their respective queue locks before waking the selector. Before run creates that selector, waking fails after the queue has already changed.',
 'After each select, drain registrations first and explicit disconnections second. Explicit removal disconnects the client, removes its registry entry and posts DISCONNECTED with reconnect=false.',
 'Accept configures a nonblocking channel with TCP_NODELAY and KEEPALIVE, registers it, constructs/attaches a client, stores the client and posts NEWCONNECT. Read and write readiness are independent checks on the selected key.',
 'An ordinary per-client I/O failure closes and removes the client and posts DISCONNECTED. Its reconnect flag is the opposite of incoming: outgoing failures request a retry, incoming failures do not.',
 'Single sends look up one UID; broadcasts visit only clients with valid greetings. shutdown sets a flag and wakes the selector. Normal loop exit closes sockets but retains client-map entries; getAllNIOClients returns a new list of those same client objects.'
], 'C++ reuses NIOClient framing and shared socket/selection-key registrations. SocketWakeup plus poll replaces the Java selector; an IPv6 dual-stack listener has an IPv4 fallback. Atomics and queue/selector locks protect native threads. Weak manager callbacks, explicit closing and getBoundPort support lifetime management and observation; the source demo main and custom JVM networking settings remain outside this API translation.', 'nio_server_differential.py','NIOServerOracle and nio_server use real loopback IPv4/IPv6 sockets and a controlled manager collector. They compare zero-, one-, 8193- and 65536-byte frames, fragmented headers, direct sends, valid-only broadcasts, explicit removal, outgoing EOF, incoming oversized-frame rejection and retained identity after shutdown. Expected traffic totals are asserted at 73750 read and 73760 written bytes for that scenario. Invalid ports and an isolated bind-collision child exercise return versus halt behavior; these finite traces do not prove all concurrent schedules.','Why does pre-start disconnect leave a queued UID despite throwing? Contrast that with shutdown, which checks whether a selector exists before waking it.')
lesson('minima/NIOManager','Coordinate listener events, connection retries, greeting exchange, message workers, traffic categories and synchronization requests.',[
 'Construction owns the server, pending-client map, traffic counters and a four-worker executor. SERVERSTARTED first initializes P2P, schedules valid configured endpoints after ten seconds, then schedules the two-minute stale-read checker.',
 'Ignore ordinary messages while Main is shutting down or restoring; SHUTDOWN still executes. CONNECT rejects known-invalid peers, creates a pending client and posts ATTEMPT. ATTEMPT checks that its UID is still pending before starting an asynchronous socket connection.',
 'RECONNECT increments attempts first. Slave mode or disabled P2P keeps retrying; ordinary mode eventually rejects a peer when alternatives exist. An otherwise isolated connection resets its attempt count. Invalid peers cancel retries, while permitted retries receive a thirty-second timer.',
 'DISCONNECTED clears both synchronization timestamps. Validity, direction, invalid-peer membership and the requested reconnect flag determine retry; slave mode can force an outgoing reconnect when no other connection to that full address exists. A retry creates a new pending client, and P2P receives the old client plus the final decision.',
 'NEWCONNECTION removes its pending UID and rejects an invalid peer. An outgoing unsent greeting marks sent=true before creating/serializing the greeting. Incoming peers wait. Received payloads become NIOMessage tasks executed in the worker pool.',
 'TXPOWREQ sends an ID request only when the database lacks it. SYNCTXBLOCK uses the last archive block or a second root lookup, skips height one and applies the configured age window for non-archive nodes. The stale checker disconnects reads older than ten minutes and schedules five-second reconnects only for valid outgoing peers.',
 'createNIOMessage writes the type byte and object bytes, without the outer length frame. sendNetworkMessage chooses one UID or broadcast and records a type/category count after sending. sendPingMessage adds the outer MiniData frame, performs a timed exchange and decodes a Greeting after discarding, rather than validating, the reply type.',
 'Normal shutdown stops/awaits workers, requests server shutdown, waits for its run loop and stops processing. hardShutDown follows a shorter path. Disconnect-all queues pending and connected removals; optional P2P removal uses advertised identity separately from the socket address.'
], 'C++ reuses NIOServer, FixedTaskExecutor, actual stream codecs and shared client objects. Factory startup establishes ownership before threads run; weak callbacks avoid owner cycles, while connector work retains its manager. Explicit service receivers represent Main/database/discovery operations that still need full-node binding. Java signed arithmetic is reproduced for archive windows; generic log/exception details and exceptional ping cleanup remain parity limits.', 'nio_manager_state_differential.py','NIOManagerStateOracle allocates an unstarted original manager and injects controlled Main/database/P2P objects. The native fixture similarly avoids connector startup. Operations compare pending/connected identity, attempt counts, packets, greeting flags, sync erasure, posted events, timers, traffic and lookup order, including failures after mutations. Assertions require packet types 0/3/13, connection timers of 5/10/30 seconds, the 120-second checker and four P2P event categories. Reconnect matrices include slave/invalid/alternative peers; archive fixtures include a root disappearing on its second lookup. Real connector dispatch, worker scheduling and complete shutdown are outside this state experiment.','If greeting creation fails after setSentGreeting(true), should another NEWCONNECTION retry the greeting? Trace the retained flag before deciding.')

lesson('minima/NIOMessage','Decode one network payload and route its protocol action, including greeting negotiation, chain synchronization and transaction relay eligibility.',[
 'Read the retained payload before checking shutdown/restoring. After reading its type, suppress ID/pulse traffic during IBD synchronization and suppress TxPoW IDs on slave nodes. Trace/category accounting occurs after these gates. A finally block clears retained data even after an early return inside dispatch.',
 'Greeting handling checks the TEST marker, updates host and advertised port, marks validity and posts P2P_CONNECTED. An incompatible incoming peer may receive our greeting before a two-second disconnect timer. Successful greeting handling records the address in the recent-IBD set before creating/sending IBD; this class itself does not implement the advertised thirty-minute set expiry.',
 'Validate received IBD before posting it to the processor. A heavier chain triggers notification and disconnect, with an optional one-second rescue timer. Sync responses with no blocks do nothing. Repeated sync requests compare only the last requested block height and update that cache before creating the response; the bandwidth gate precedes it.',
 'TxPoW ID/request messages perform database lookup and send a request or object. A received new TxPoW needs a local tip. Wrong chain ID, basic/signature failure or excessive state size disconnects; later difficulty, relay, time, size, mempool and MMR checks usually disable rebroadcast while still posting the object. A failed monotonic script instead returns before posting.',
 'For eligible received blocks, request missing transaction IDs and inspect at most 512 stored ancestors. A separate ten-minute per-peer throttle permits inspecting up to 256 local tip ancestors for missing transactions; synthetic UIDs 0x00 and 0x01 skip that latter scan. DECIMAL32 rounding precedes the 0.01 difficulty-ratio decision.',
 'Pulse handling rejects more than 1000 IDs and prepends missing IDs to a request list, reversing their encounter order. Requests are sent only after finding a local crossover. No crossover records invalid peer addresses and disconnects; its diagnostic port selection preserves the source’s -1 quirk.',
 'General text is gated by ALLOW_GEN_MESSAGE. P2P text is decoded before checking P2P_ENABLED and is parsed as an object; absent peer greeting delays its event ten seconds. Ordinary PING only consumes data. SINGLE_PING replies with chain/peer details; fields named 50block and 50hash actually use getParent(100). Its type-name conversion remains UNKNOWN_11.',
 'Archive request -1 returns an empty connectivity-test IBD; ordinary archive requests build data. ARCHIVE_SINGLE_REQ has an inactive body, and received ARCHIVE_DATA is logged then ignored. Slave TxBlock messages use database/tree fallback, optionally archive lookup for requests, post blocks before seeking a missing parent, and throttle mining after resetting the PRNG.',
 'MegaMMR requests require the feature flag, decode sync data and call the external MegaMMR builder. Defined Maxima types, SINGLE_PONG and MegaMMR responses have no receive branch here and fall through to unknown-message logging. Ordinary caught exceptions are logged; decoding does not require consuming every trailing payload byte.'
], 'C++ reuses actual TxPoWChecker, TxPoWGenerator, IBD, chain-search and binary codec implementations. Shared payload retention and a scope guard replace stream/finally ownership; explicit Main/database/discovery/processor/miner receivers expose missing runtime bindings. Decimal comparison preserves the tested Java rounding decision, and atomic/concurrent fields protect native state without establishing every source interleaving. Logging uses native diagnostic output and does not reproduce Java MINIMALOG notifications.', 'nio_message_differential.py','NIOMessageOracle and nio_message execute actual dispatch with Java-generated binary payloads and controlled external receivers. They compare queued reply bytes, peer/processor/miner events, client mutations, traffic categories, retained-data cleanup and sync caches. The corpus covers all 256 type bytes, truncated envelopes, greeting repetition, JSON types, real script/signature/MMR decisions, 512/256 scan boundaries, getParent(100), and heavier-chain rescue. Explicit assertions check reply/event categories and the five difficulty-boundary relay decisions [true,false,false,false,true]. Generic caught errors and logs are excluded; no sockets, database writes or miner are started, and successful MegaMMR service binding plus exact live-clock boundaries remain open.','A TxPoW passes basic validation but fails the non-monotonic script check. Trace processing and broadcasting separately. Why would dropping it immediately be a different algorithm?')
